meta {
  name: Gated site — open a sign-in window
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/connectors/{{scrapeConnector}}/browser/login
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
}

docs {
  Starts a sign-in — the response's `login.mode` says which kind: a real Chromium window
  **on the machine running QuickJoiner** (`"local"`, when it has a display), or a headless
  session streamed back via requests 8–10 (`"remote"`, e.g. Docker/cloud with no display at
  all). Either way the session is then reused for every sync. Returns immediately (it is a
  background job) — poll `GET .../browser/session` to see when it lands.

  409 when a sign-in is already running for this connector. 409 with "Playwright is not
  installed" only when the `browser` extra genuinely isn't there — a headless host on its
  own no longer refuses (that's what request 8's screencast is for).

  The URL comes from the connector's own `start_urls`, never from the request body: this
  route must not become a way to make the server open an arbitrary page.

  Most SSO sign-ins issue a **session cookie**, which a browser profile cannot retain on
  its own — QuickJoiner captures those explicitly (from the open window, or from the
  headless page for a remote session), which is what makes the sign-in stick.
}
